(TIF) S3 Fig. Outline of the employed RosettaLigand design protocol. The protocol starts with a small ligand position perturbation followed by optimization of the protein:ligand interface. Amino acids are allowed to change their identity only if it results in a significant decrease in energy, defined through a “favor native” bonus (1 REU in the used protocol). The sequence design step is followed by reevaluation of the ligand position using high resolution docking protocol. The final model is scored and saved for further analysis.   
(TIF)
S4 Fig. Green to blue fluorescence signal ratio in nuclei of living HeLa Kyoto cells transiently transfected with H2B-DiB1-TagBFP or H2B-DiB-RM-TagBFP in presence of different concentrations of M739. Represented are data for 35–40 cells from the same field of view across the whole ligand concentration range. Box whiskers indicate standard deviation, horizontal lines within boxes indicate median values, circles indicate outliers. (TIF)
